    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34463" root="فلج" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلْجَانٌ</span></b> , [said to be] from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلْجٌ</span> signifying “ a
certain measure of capacity, ” [but app. from the
Pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِنْجَان</span>,] <i>A</i> [<i>small porcelain</i> or <i>earthenware</i>]
<i>cup out of which coffee &amp;c. is drunk;</i> commonly
pronounced by the vulgar <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِنْجَان</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِنْجَال</span> [from
the Pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">پِنْگَان</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">پِنْگَال</span>, and also called
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِلْجَانَةٌ</span></b> , vulgarly <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِنْجَانَة</span>; and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيَالَجَة</span></b> : (see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَوْمَلَةٌ</span>:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلَاجِينُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَنَاجِينُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَنَاجِيلُ</span>].
(TA.)

